What is Food Grade Avocado Oil?
Food grade avocado oil is a high-quality edible oil extracted from avocado fruit pulp, meeting stringent food safety and quality standards for culinary and food manufacturing applications. This premium oil is characterized by its rich monounsaturated fat content, high smoke point, and neutral flavor profile, making it suitable for diverse uses including cooking, dressings, marinades, and food processing. The market primarily consists of extra virgin, virgin, and refined avocado oil variants, each with distinct processing methods and quality parameters.
Market growth is driven by increasing consumer demand for healthy cooking oils, rising awareness of avocado oil's nutritional benefits, and expanding applications in the food industry. Processing capacity stands at approximately 85% utilization across 28 dedicated facilities nationwide, with cold-pressed extraction methods dominating 78% of production. The sector has seen significant advancements in manufacturing efficiency (52% improvement through automation) and sustainability (55% reduction in water usage), further strengthening its market position.
